{pad:meta title='Widgets'/}

<p>{app:tag 'widget:tabs'/} puts an interactive part on the page - tabs, an accordion, a carousel, a modal,
a dropdown, a toast and more, {pad:echo php:count(padWidgetTypes())/} of them. Every one is built on
the server and works without JavaScript; where a widget has a script it only makes it handier,
and it is written once per page with the CSP nonce. Every widget is a file of
<code>pad/subs/widgets/types/</code>, and the files there are the widgets there are.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/widgets_1'/}

<h2>Select a widget</h2>

<p>The qualified name selects the widget, and its first parameter is the widget's own value: <code>{pad:open/}widget:toast 'Saved'/{pad:close/}</code>.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/widgets_2'/}

<h2>What the browser does itself</h2>

<p>Each widget stands on what HTML and CSS can do: radio buttons and CSS for tabs and the wizard,
<code>&lt;details&gt;</code> for the accordion, a <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> for the modal, the
drawer and the toast, the <code>popover</code> attribute for the dropdown, <code>:hover</code>
and <code>:focus-within</code> for the tooltip, <code>:target</code> for the carousel's links and
the lightbox, the CSS resize grip for a split pane. The keyboard works because the browser's own controls are underneath; the scripts
add the arrow keys of a menu, Escape on a tooltip, the focus of a lightbox, the bar of a split
pane.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/widgets_3'/}

<h2>Items made by a loop</h2>

<p>Tabs, an accordion, a carousel, a wizard and a lightbox take {app:tag 'tab'/} items. A tab hands
its content to the nearest of them above it, so it may stand in an <code>{pad:open/}pad:if{pad:close/}</code>
or in a loop over data - a step per row of a <code>{pad:open/}pad:data{pad:close/}</code> store here.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/widgets_4'/}

<ul>
  <li>The colours are custom properties on <code>.pad-&lt;widget&gt;</code> -
  <code>--pad-tabs-accent</code>, <code>--pad-toast-success</code> and their like - with light
  and dark defaults.</li>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}widget:copy{pad:close/}</code> runs the copy widget; <code>{pad:open/}pad:tab{pad:close/}</code>
  is a built-in tag too.</li>
  <li>A name that is no widget, an unknown option value and a widget without what it needs - a
  name, a label, a tab - are errors under the strict check.</li>
</ul>
